## Annex D — Maintenance instructions and wear parts (extract)

Wear parts excluded from warranty: door gaskets, drain hoses, filter-driers, fan belts. Preventive service interval: every 1,500 operating hours or 12 months, whichever comes first. Marine coating package: fresh-water wash of the coil every 6 months. Coolant: R-452A only; charge weight 3.9 kg for a Standard Unit and 4.6 kg for an X Unit.

## Annex E — Acceptance specification (extract)

| Test | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Pull-down +20.0 °C to −18.0 °C | not more than 118 minutes |
| Stability at −18.0 °C, 4 hours | ±0.3 K |
| Electrical consumption after pull-down | not more than 6.8 kW |
| GlideLink handshake with KC-Hub 200 | within 90 seconds |

## Annex G — Service credits for hotline response (extract)

If the remote diagnosis under Article 7.3 is later than 4 hours, the Supplier gives the following credit against the next Spare Parts invoice, per late response.

| Delay beyond 4 hours | Credit |
|---|---|
| up to 2 hours | EUR 150 |
| more than 2 and up to 8 hours | EUR 420 |
| more than 8 hours | EUR 950 |

The aggregate hotline credits in a calendar quarter are capped at EUR 6,500. A credit is not payable where the delay was caused by the Buyer's failure to provide access to the Unit's log.

